  "reason": "The alias diagnostic is fundamentally an action-bisimulation / equivalence failure test, which is well-established in MDP state-abstraction literature (DeepMDP, DBC) and action-semantic gap analyses (arXiv:2610.06582, WAV). The uniform 93–96% split rate across baseline, WAV, Hard-Oracle, and Random models demonstrates that this metric reflects standard unconstrained latent capacity rather than an exploitable security vulnerability. Without an operationalized threat model showing how an unprivileged adversary exploits this split to cause downstream closed-loop controller failure, it carries under 10% likelihood of novelty acceptance at ICLR."
}

